title CF-M08 — Local activity versus selected calendar synchronization
start
:CF-M08-S01\nInitiating actor\nUser requests a local activity\naction or a separate agreed\nsynchronization action.;
if (CF-M08-S02\nCurrent actor can perform\nrequested local activity operation?) then (yes)
if (CF-M08-S03\nRequest is local activity change\nonly?) then (yes)
:CF-M08-S04\nUser / System\nIdentify local time meaning,\nassociations and intended change;
:CF-M08-S05\nSystem\nSave permitted local operation\nwithout implied provider write;
:CF-M08-S06\nSystem\nUse CF-M17 to classify actual\nresult; return only evidence-\nsupported effect;
stop
else (no)
:CF-M08-S07\nUser\nExplicitly select intended\nmapping/action;
if (CF-M08-S08\nRequested action is local unlink?) then (yes)
:CF-M08-S09\nSystem\nRemove permitted local association\nonly; do not delete provider event\nor require provider write access;
:CF-M08-S10\nSystem\nUse CF-M17 to classify actual\nresult; return only evidence-\nsupported effect;
stop
else (no)
if (CF-M08-S11\nCurrent provider\nidentity/capability and mapping\ncontext valid?) then (yes)
:CF-M08-S12\nSystem\nCompare relevant local/provider\nversions and field authority;
if (CF-M08-S13\nConflicting concurrent changes\nexist?) then (yes)
:CF-M08-S14\nSystem\nShow conflict; require explicit\nresolution before overwrite;
stop
else (no)
:CF-M08-S15\nSystem\nPerform only intended permitted\nsync/provider action;
if (CF-M08-S16\nActual matching result confirmed?) then (yes)
:CF-M08-S17\nSystem\nRecord truthful mapping/freshness\nor provider removal result;
stop
else (no)
:CF-M08-S18\nSystem\nKeep stale/failed/unknown\ndistinction; reconcile before\nfurther effects;
stop
endif
endif
else (no)
:CF-M08-S19\nSystem\nBlock dependent provider action;\nretained copies stay visibly stale\nas applicable;
stop
endif
endif
endif
else (no)
:CF-M08-S20\nSystem\nDeny before prohibited effect or\nprotected disclosure; report unmet\ngate;
stop
endif
legend bottom
A: accepted profile core only. Other policy detail: P / proposed refinement.
Step IDs identify full descriptions in the activity view.
Logical ordering; no atomicity, runtime, timing or execution proof.
